			"notes": "- Inline modifier is now used, creating byte-code horrors, but significantly reducing overall overhead\n- New builder method `aegisCommand`, the old style of `AegisCommandBuilder(\"value\") { ... }.build()` is depreciated\n- Aegis will now throw an error in the log if one of your command tree paths does not end in an executes block\n- You can now enable debugging for executes blocks, printing a stacktrace when they fail (pass `true` as a parameter)\n- `executes` in now implicit, and will return 1 if no errors are throw, or 0 if there are\n    - If you want to specify the return yourself, use `executesExplicit`\n- More supported arguments\n    - Identifier\n    - Vec2\n    - Text"
		},
